From: BedrockOnLinux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] windows.storage: implement Windows.Storage.Pickers.FileSavePicker

Every export Minecraft offers -- a structure block's, a world's, the album's
PDF and ZIP, a model's GLB -- goes through AppPlatform_GameCorePC::pickFile,
which activates Windows.Storage.Pickers.FileSavePicker, hands it the game
window through IInitializeWithWindow, fills SuggestedFileName,
SuggestedStartLocation and FileTypeChoices, calls PickSaveFileAsync and reads
the chosen path back through IStorageItem. Nothing registered or implemented
the class, so RoActivateInstance failed with REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG and the
export spun on its loading screen for ever (BedrockOnLinux issue #167).

Implement it in windows.storage.dll beside the WinAppSDK open picker. The
dialog is GetSaveFileNameW, owned by the window the caller initialized the
picker with, filtered by the file-type choices in the order they were
inserted, opening in the suggested location with the suggested name, and
appending the default extension -- DefaultFileExtension, else the first
choice's first extension -- to a name typed without one. It asks before
replacing a file. Like the single-file open picker it is modal, so
PickSaveFileAsync returns an operation that is already complete and a
completion handler runs as soon as it is set. As on Windows, the picked file
exists afterwards, empty unless it was there before, in which case it is left
untouched for its caller to write; a dismissed dialog completes with no file.
The file is handed over as the Windows.Storage.StorageFile that
windows.storage.applicationdata.dll serves.

FileTypeChoices is an IMap<HSTRING, IVector<HSTRING> *> of the caller's own
vectors. windows.storage.pickers.idl declares the Windows.Storage.Pickers
types; its PickerLocationId shares its C enumerator names with the WinAppSDK
one, so savepicker.c is the only file that sees it.
---
